Create workflow engine, where we want to support 3 kinds of task - sleep, console where you can just log something and third could be to make an http call and print the http status of the response. 
As a user we can trigger any task in the workflow.
Workflow is a basically adding one or multiple tasks and then triggering them any number of times. 
Assume will trigger them via API. We can discuss about crons at end (bonus)


FR
Create a workflow with uniqueId
Add multiple tasks to workflow
Support sleep, console and http tasks
Execute tasks sequentially in their order
Trigger the workflow multiple times
Track workflow execution status
Handle task failure without crashing workflow - As of now if task fails fail the workflow itself
Support concurrent workflow execution
Same workflow can be retriggered during inprocess status. New instance to be created for the new workflow that is triggered

Assumption
If task fails then fail entire workflow
Each trigger will have new executionId

NFRs
Extensibility - Strategy pattern for tasks
Thread safety for in-memory-repo
ThreadPoolExecutor for independent workflow runs


